A||||43||batboy||fell in love with a Fiero girl||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||05-02-2000||10:55 PM||||I was running some errands after work on I-170 (Topeka by-pass) while driving my black 85 Fiero GT and saw another black 85 Fiero GT that looked identical to mine right down to the wing in my rearview. It was running in the left lane and would soon be passing me. I watched in my mirror as this nice, freshly waxed beauty pulled up beside me. I turned to look at the driver, smiled, and gave them the peace sign. I was quite surprised to see a young beautiful woman smiling back at me and giving me the peace sign in return too. I nearly melted. It was love at first sight, both the girl and the car!<P>She completed her pass and switched into the right lane, so I speeded up to pace her. Alas, a couple miles later she turned down an exit ramp while I continued on. As I pulled up even with her for a second time, I looked over again. She flashed me the prettiest big smile and waved with her left hand. Oh my God, no ring! It was too late for me to exit! ***sigh***<P>Now I'm going to be like Richard Drefus in the movie American Graffitti, except I'll be constantly cruising and looking for the mystery brunette in a 85 Fiero GT instead of a blonde in a 55 Thunderbird. ***sigh again***||||reg||1
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||05-02-2000||11:32 PM||||::sigh::<P>Shoulda chased her down or atleast followed her 24/7, but that's called stalking, atleast that's what the jugde called it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||05-02-2000||11:48 PM||||Even with that brief encounter at 70-75 mph, I know so much about her. Very lovely, nice figure (sure I looked, I'm a man, right), happy (nice smile), single (no wedding ring), friendly (she wave to me), a good driver (she signaled lane changes and drove that Fiero like a pro) intelligent (drives a Fiero), and has great taste (drives a very nice Fiero GT). ***sigh***||||reg||1
